id: pm-web-xucb
title: Resolve pm-web full development audit through unpatched braces and fast-glob
description: "CLI/ops/changelog2026.10.4 has clean production audit but four high full-audit entries through fast-glob/micromatch/braces and pm-ops. GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm affects every published braces3 release. pm-ops declares fast-glob^3.3.3 as an optional peer; its duplication entrypoint statically imports that peer, so this consumer must supply it. Removing the repository dependency makes audit clean but breaks the required canonical gate. Retain exact latest pins and audit/gate requirements pending a compatible clean peer chain."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-04T13:45:56.448Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-10T04:08:30.465Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "Full npm audit and npm audit --omit=dev both zero on exact required pins; canonical pm-ops duplication and full package release gates pass without suppressions, skipped tests or forced breaking overrides."
severity: high
repro_steps: npm ci; npm audit --json; npm ls braces micromatch fast-glob pm-ops; npm view braces version
expected_result: All audit requirements clean with functional canonical gates.
actual_result: "SDK2026.10.9 candidate: production audit0; current-author linked full npm audit executes and rejects four high development entries for GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm. Installed and registry-latest compatible chain is pm-ops2026.10.6,fast-glob3.3.3,micromatch4.0.8,braces3.0.3. No safe patched compatible version is available; suggested pm-ops2026.9.13 is a downgrade. Retain required peer and all gates; owner remains unclosed."
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-04T13:56:03.219Z",codex-sol,"Exact installed CLI/ops/changelog2026.10.4: npm audit --omit=dev --json exits0 with allzero; npm audit --json exits1 with fourhigh deventries. GitHub open Dependabotalerts returns[]; no openalertsilentlyclosed. Published braceslatest3.0.3 affected by GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm; no3.0.4published. Removing direct unusedfastglob was independently attempted in pm-graph certification and auditsclean, but canonical pm-ops10.4 duplication then throws ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND because its dist/duplication.js staticallyimports undeclaredfastglob. Keep latestexactpins andfunctionalcanonicalgate; blockerownedhereuntilcompatibleupstreamtooltreeclean. Do not force downgrade/suppressaudit."
  "2026-10-04T14:01:53.564Z",codex-sol,"The initial linked npm audit commands hit runner-injected EALLOWSCRIPTS, so their exit1 is execution failure, not vulnerability evidence. Direct same-source npm audit --omit=dev --json recheckexit0/allzero; full recheckexit1/fourhigh. Replace the two new linked commands with child-scoped env -u npm_config_allow_scripts -u NPM_CONFIG_ALLOW_SCRIPTS wrappers; this changes no audit selection/threshold and no project or user npm configuration."
  "2026-10-04T14:13:52.444Z",codex-sol,"Correction after complete installed manifest inspection: pm-ops2026.10.4 declares fast-glob^3.3.3 as an optional peer (peerDependenciesMeta.optional=true), rather than a direct dependency. The earlier undeclared-import wording was inaccurate. The duplication entrypoint statically imports that optional peer, so a consumer using this gate must provide it; removing it cannot certify the consumer. Clarify description/document; no missing-declaration defect claimed. Full development audit4high remains, prod audit0, functional fullgate411/411 and required consumer pins unchanged."
  "2026-10-10T03:17:13.905Z",codex-sol,"Fresh npm registry checks: braces3.0.3, micromatch4.0.8, fast-glob3.3.3 and pm-ops2026.10.6 remain latest and match installed resolutions. npm audit still reports four high development entries for GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm through braces/micromatch/fast-glob/pm-ops. No safe patched compatible release available; suggested pm-ops2026.9.13 is a tool downgrade. Retain functional required peer chain, no audit suppression or forced breaking override; production audit remains a separate gate."
